NFG 1 R "Harsanyi (1968), Table 8" { "Player 1" "Player 2" } { { "y11" "y12" "y21" "y22" } { "z11" "z12" "z21" "z22" } }
"The normal form of the two-person zero-sum Bayesian game of Section 9, giving Player 1's
expected payoff (Player 2 receives the negative). A strategy y<n><t> of Player 1 plays y<n> if
Player 1 is in class a1 and y<t> if in a2; a strategy z<u><v> of Player 2 plays z<u> if in b1 and
z<v> if in b2. The only saddle point is (y21,z11), with value 8.8; there is none in mixed
strategies. It is the unique Bayesian equilibrium of the game."

